07:13.460 --> 07:16.640
put it— there's holding companies that will hold that number and forward it. Oh,

07:17.140 --> 07:20.300
just hold the number, not keep it active? Yeah, well, the number stays active and

07:20.800 --> 07:24.020
they put it in basically a bank. We can look into that. Yeah, that would

07:24.520 --> 07:28.060
just— that number, if you— some reason we got all kinds of

07:28.560 --> 07:32.100
feedback today, but if it was, uh, if that was the case In

07:32.600 --> 07:35.320
order to forward it, that's different than the hold. The hold just freezes the number.

07:35.820 --> 07:37.560
It would have to be an active line, which at the minimum I think is

07:38.060 --> 07:41.760
$9, $10, $11 maybe.

07:42.260 --> 07:45.020
But that's trying to keep the confusion, you know what I mean? Yeah, I know

07:45.520 --> 07:49.060
what you're saying. So really the question is, is that a desire of council to

07:49.560 --> 07:52.740
do that? I don't want to have 2 phones. I think that sucks. Would the

07:53.240 --> 07:56.140
