If we're talking about steeple, I mean, that's probably something that we're

57:38.770 --> 57:43.858
having a different discussion about, but this is This

57:43.906 --> 57:48.004
is a recreation hall, and if

57:48.085 --> 57:51.311
we do it here, that could easily be something that we have to

57:51.811 --> 57:55.087
say yes to again in a different location. I think we've set a seating

57:55.507 --> 57:58.767
height of 35, unless we're viewing this as

57:59.267 --> 58:02.412
a commercial use now, which I don't think that's the case, in which case that

58:02.494 --> 58:05.708
changes that. I don't know that it's really identified

58:06.393 --> 58:10.171
that I can find. Specifically, this is a little bit of a gray area.

58:12.460 --> 58:16.162
But I don't think they want to have a commercial zone on

58:16.275 --> 58:20.657
this. That wouldn't be beneficial to tax collection. I think

58:21.157 --> 58:25.481
to me, 35 probably would not be unless there's an

58:25.981 --> 58:29.322
appetite by the city to create a special use

58:29.516 --> 58:32.668
when it's an ecclesiastical entity.

58:34.780 --> 58:37.820
And I agree with Councilmember Wright,

58:38.320 --> 58:42.360
or Wood here, because— so if we allow that here, I don't see

58:42.860 --> 58:46.300
how if another ecclesiastical, like another— Like the

58:46.800 --> 58:48.340
LDS Church. Like the LDS Church, for instance. So say the LDS Church came in

58:48.840 --> 58:51.100
and applied and said, okay, we want 40 feet. How would we be able to

58:51.600 --> 58:55.280
say no at that point? And I worry, I do worry about some precedents

58:55.780 --> 58:59.050
with that. I think that height is something that is I

58:59.550 --> 59:03.250
think that's a pretty ubiquitous rule that needs to apply through the city.

59:04.730 --> 59:07.960
I'm more flexible on pathways. I think that's— I don't have any issues with that.

59:08.330 --> 59:11.890
The fact that this is right up against that Walmart, I'm not as

59:12.390 --> 59:15.820
concerned about the architectural features on that side as well.

59:15.990 --> 59:19.510
That is a reasonable request, but I think the height does

59:20.010 --> 59:23.770
open up other issues that we could bind ourselves unwittingly

59:24.270 --> 59:27.620
as a council. Councilmember White, can I speak to

59:28.120 --> 59:31.300
that? Mayor, may I speak to that just a minute? Yeah, go ahead. I'll just

59:31.800 --> 59:34.800
say that, I mean, I've had a chance to probably digest this a little bit

59:35.300 --> 59:38.500
deeper than most council. I know that most of you are seeing this for

59:39.000 --> 59:42.200
the first time, and I've seen it for a few weeks. It came before DRC

59:42.700 --> 59:46.640
and had a chance to think a little bit about it. And part of the

59:47.140 --> 59:50.040
issue, as I talked to Mr. Baker, that they're having is that they want to

59:50.540 --> 59:54.320
do both basketball volleyball in here, and they'd like and have designed

59:54.820 --> 59:58.340
the building to be that tall, recognizing that they don't want to bring

59:58.840 --> 01:00:03.040
plans forward if there's really no appetite by council to consider

01:00:03.540 --> 01:00:06.920
making an exception in the

01:00:07.420 --> 01:00:10.940
only way that is available to them through development agreements. So we're not

01:00:11.440 --> 01:00:14.660
talking about changing code, we're not talking about a variance, we're not talking about anything

01:00:15.160 --> 01:00:18.740
like that. The code would still stand for all other uses. And in

01:00:19.240 --> 01:00:22.460
his very specific instance, just like you said,

01:00:22.960 --> 01:00:27.100
Councilmember Whitey, it's a pretty unique location in the city with

01:00:27.600 --> 01:00:31.140
a big box store directly to

01:00:31.640 --> 01:00:36.300
the east. And so the question in my mind became—

01:00:36.800 --> 01:00:38.560
and I listened to Councilmember Wood and I say, look, we don't want to adjust

01:00:39.060 --> 01:00:42.340
the skyline. And my question is really—

01:00:42.840 --> 01:00:46.040
What's the detrimental impact by considering that through development agreement?

01:00:46.410 --> 01:00:49.990
I'm really interested in hearing that because from my perspective, I don't see a

01:00:50.490 --> 01:00:54.050
lot. But that's why this is before council, is to really allow the applicant

01:00:54.550 --> 01:00:57.410
to kind of take the temperature of the council to see if there's even a

01:00:57.910 --> 01:01:01.600
willingness to consider this making an exception through development agreement. If there is,

01:01:02.030 --> 01:01:05.490
I would be probably more favorable to that. And if there's

01:01:05.990 --> 01:01:09.190
not, then, then he'll at least know the direction he needs

01:01:09.690 --> 01:01:11.930
to go to be able to bring the project forward. Thank you.

01:01:12.220 --> 01:01:16.320
So I'm just trying to think what are some other buildings

01:01:16.820 --> 01:01:20.100
that are existing in the city that might have that use. It's probably going to

01:01:20.600 --> 01:01:23.860
be the school, frankly. You're probably talking about their gyms. Do we know the

01:01:24.360 --> 01:01:27.920
height of the gyms in our middle schools or elementary schools?

01:01:28.420 --> 01:01:31.930
I don't. I don't know if that's something we ever look at.

01:01:31.980 --> 01:01:35.080
So I would say that's probably a good place to start. Let's figure that

01:01:35.580 --> 01:01:39.460
out. Maybe that's, maybe that's where we find the common ground in

01:01:39.960 --> 01:01:43.550
that, that the different Do we

01:01:44.050 --> 01:01:47.090
consider civic schools educational use?

01:01:47.590 --> 01:01:51.190
Institutional educational civic uses to wrap that

01:01:51.690 --> 01:01:54.840
in? Because I don't want to make exceptions,

01:01:55.250 --> 01:01:58.950
frankly. I don't like that. I mean, I understand what you're saying, Brandon,

01:01:59.450 --> 01:02:02.730
about MDAs, but first in usually creates

01:02:03.230 --> 01:02:05.530
a problem for us down the road. We have experience with that. I'm not saying

01:02:06.030 --> 01:02:09.472
that. Rather than just saying, okay, we understand the use, what they're trying to do,

01:02:09.908 --> 01:02:13.425
let's address it so that the next person comes in, we already have a thing

01:02:13.458 --> 01:02:16.923
in place that we're addressing it so that we're even-handed in

01:02:17.423 --> 01:02:21.577
the way that we're addressing this. Because generally speaking, if we already

01:02:22.077 --> 01:02:25.036
are there at 40 feet of the schools, then why does it matter?

01:02:28.232 --> 01:02:31.370
I think one— wait for you to finish that,

01:02:31.484 --> 01:02:34.952
but just as a thought as well, You said civic,

01:02:34.984 --> 01:02:38.632
and of course schools, whatever, but you know height is gonna at least

01:02:39.132 --> 01:02:42.267
be a discussion. I don't know where everybody's gonna land, but when we started in

01:02:42.315 --> 01:02:44.795
City Hall, some of our own, you know.

01:02:45.939 --> 01:02:49.159
So I think, and that also could be

01:02:49.643 --> 01:02:54.241
specific to a downtown district, which is different as well because downtown's

01:02:54.741 --> 01:02:58.390
different than everywhere. I think you can make it as

01:02:58.503 --> 01:03:01.181
an exception in a certain area, possibly, but— Yeah.

01:03:01.927 --> 01:03:05.488
Anyway. I guess—

01:03:05.988 --> 01:03:09.386
sorry. I think the thing is, to my

01:03:09.886 --> 01:03:13.750
fellow council members, some of the things that we have said when people

01:03:14.250 --> 01:03:17.439
have wanted us to consider higher buildings for hotels, or they

01:03:17.487 --> 01:03:20.343
wanted us to consider, you know, X, Y, or Z,

01:03:20.936 --> 01:03:23.776
we don't want to put it in code is usually what we say,

01:03:24.546 --> 01:03:28.620
because we're willing to look at the specific circumstance

01:03:28.878 --> 01:03:32.605
and weigh the circumstance with the impact and all of those things.

01:03:33.135 --> 01:03:36.541
And I feel like as a practice,

01:03:36.831 --> 01:03:40.542
we as a body tend to make these choices

01:03:41.042 --> 01:03:45.057
and changes through development agreement rather than code because

01:03:45.557 --> 01:03:48.849
there's sometimes that we just don't want that code spread far

01:03:48.977 --> 01:03:52.640
and wide throughout the city and it's very specific instances.

01:03:53.090 --> 01:03:56.860
So for me, I really look at

01:03:57.360 --> 01:04:00.619
this and think, if this was built in a neighborhood with apartments, we probably wouldn't

01:04:01.119 --> 01:04:04.636
even bat an eye at it. Like, and it's a special circumstance.

01:04:05.152 --> 01:04:08.992
It's a church and recreation building nestled

01:04:09.104 --> 01:04:12.541
behind a Walmart in a bunch of homes that

01:04:12.718 --> 01:04:15.145
are the people who are going to use this specific property.

01:04:18.837 --> 01:04:22.266
If it limits their ability to be able to do what

01:04:22.574 --> 01:04:25.182
they want and need to do in the space,

01:04:25.798 --> 01:04:27.839
then I think we should really look at it and say,

01:04:29.058 --> 01:04:32.400
is it going to impact the neighbors? Is it going to change the nature

01:04:32.900 --> 01:04:36.337
or character of the space or hurt the city in some way?

01:04:36.755 --> 01:04:40.024
And if it doesn't, then I think we should consider it and lean

01:04:40.088 --> 01:04:43.542
more into property rights and letting them use their property

01:04:44.042 --> 01:04:46.414
to its fullest capacity. Okay.

01:04:47.100 --> 01:04:50.580
You've got two different arguments there. If we're talking about property rights, those have already

01:04:51.080 --> 01:04:54.370
been established. There's a code that they follow; they don't meet that requirement.

01:04:54.640 --> 01:04:58.420
So the answer is no. I'm trying to find a solution that goes forward that

01:04:58.920 --> 01:05:02.600
creates an even standard. The next entity

01:05:03.100 --> 01:05:06.380
that is a religious entity that wants to come and build something that has

01:05:06.880 --> 01:05:10.420
a recreational use, what is that standard going to be? If we're trying to do

01:05:10.920 --> 01:05:14.030
it so narrow that it can only exist. In this particular

01:05:14.530 --> 01:05:18.130
neighborhood on this particular lot. I think that's a dangerous precedent

01:05:18.630 --> 01:05:22.410
because overall I think I've been pretty upfront about I want this

01:05:22.910 --> 01:05:26.290
project to happen. But I think we have to be careful when we start being

01:05:26.790 --> 01:05:30.030
too specific where everything has to be this council is going to make this decision

01:05:30.530 --> 01:05:34.070
because the next council may not have the same expertise in land use

01:05:34.570 --> 01:05:37.450
and it's very easy for them to just arbitrarily just start saying yes to things

01:05:37.950 --> 01:05:41.320
without any really a baseline for us. So for me,

01:05:41.820 --> 01:05:45.460
I'm trying to find— The fact that you said volleyball, that was actually

01:05:45.960 --> 01:05:47.760
one of the questions I was going to ask. It sounds to me like we're

01:05:48.260 --> 01:05:50.870
trying to get some height on that. That's why I asked about the schools.

01:05:51.580 --> 01:05:53.980
Basketball, that's not going to be a problem. There's plenty of height for that.

01:05:54.480 --> 01:05:57.720
But volleyball, that's a problem. You've got a ceiling problem where you'd be hitting that.

01:05:58.220 --> 01:06:01.920
So I think this is a discussion that's not even on there.

01:06:02.420 --> 01:06:05.520
I think let's get some information to bring back to us and find out what

01:06:06.020 --> 01:06:09.179
the height of these other buildings are. And then let's put something in place that

01:06:09.679 --> 01:06:12.968
allows for this to happen in these specific circumstances.

01:06:13.048 --> 01:06:16.886
I'm not looking to say no. I'm saying that for this specific

01:06:17.386 --> 01:06:21.767
circumstance, in this way, we can say yes specifically

01:06:22.267 --> 01:06:25.540
to this. And that way, when the next applicant comes to us and says we

01:06:26.040 --> 01:06:29.667
want to build a recreation hall as part of our ecclesiastical whatever,

01:06:29.988 --> 01:06:32.525
it's very easy because we've already laid it all out for them.

01:06:39.778 --> 01:06:42.928
So, Steven, I'm going to come to you because we do need to get through

01:06:42.961 --> 01:06:46.143
some more other things. This is a— we kind of need to move on.

01:06:46.433 --> 01:06:49.572
Are you clear on where we're at, or do we need some— No,

01:06:50.298 --> 01:06:55.073
I'd be curious if Councilmember Huish has any comments on that. Oh, I didn't— yeah,

01:06:56.106 --> 01:06:57.767
Councilmember Huish, if you want to weigh in.

01:06:59.835 --> 01:07:03.187
Well, I can see both sides, both arguments.

01:07:03.283 --> 01:07:08.030
We want to be consistent throughout the city. My questions are, are there any

01:07:08.191 --> 01:07:11.863
surrounding properties where their views would be obstructed

01:07:12.264 --> 01:07:16.097
or in the way? I tend to lean

01:07:16.597 --> 01:07:20.860
towards following code, but I also think

01:07:21.325 --> 01:07:23.651
there could be exceptions made. For example?

01:07:23.940 --> 01:07:28.546
Let's say that the LDS Church wanted to build a temple somewhere in

01:07:29.252 --> 01:07:32.783
Eagle Mountain. Would we have that same requirement

01:07:33.283 --> 01:07:37.357
that they keep the top of the temple at 40 feet? I'm just throwing out

01:07:37.857 --> 01:07:41.529
a specific example where, you know,

01:07:41.545 --> 01:07:46.296
there could be other religious exemptions that

01:07:46.344 --> 01:07:50.597
would be made. So that same question

01:07:51.097 --> 01:07:53.683
was through my mind, but the reality of it is I don't think that They're

01:07:54.183 --> 01:07:56.785
stating this is their house of worship, this is a recreation space.

01:07:57.646 --> 01:07:59.335
I think we want to make sure we keep those separately.

01:08:01.650 --> 01:08:04.884
For anybody who's trying to do a house of worship, I think that

01:08:05.079 --> 01:08:07.208
is a different category than what we're talking about here.

01:08:08.490 --> 01:08:11.806
I'm sorry, can you repeat that? Being a religious organization owning property shouldn't

01:08:12.306 --> 01:08:16.186
give you specific development rights to

01:08:16.686 --> 01:08:20.310
a building specifically, in my opinion. Houses of worship should

01:08:20.810 --> 01:08:25.170
have a standard that we follow that applies to everybody. Recreation centers that belong

01:08:25.670 --> 01:08:28.910
to a 501 or belong to a

01:08:29.410 --> 01:08:33.670
religious organization or a private organization ought to have a standard that we're following.

01:08:36.950 --> 01:08:40.620
I'm one person, by the way. If nobody else agrees with me, that's fine too.

01:08:40.730 --> 01:08:44.350
I think it's not going to hurt to do what you asked Commissioner Wood

01:08:44.850 --> 01:08:48.000
to to get some of the measurements. If we can get to a yes and

01:08:48.500 --> 01:08:52.430
make a code adjustment that gives us a good framework moving forward,

01:08:52.739 --> 01:08:55.940
great. And if we can't, then we can kind of battle

01:08:56.440 --> 01:08:58.420
that out and get it to the place that we need to get to as

01:08:58.920 --> 01:09:02.300
a body. So I'm inclined just to send Steven on his way

01:09:02.800 --> 01:09:06.300
and tell him, bring us back information and let's move forward with that

01:09:06.800 --> 01:09:10.740
discussion. Well, I'm kind of curious what we at Legacy Center was,

01:09:11.240 --> 01:09:13.394
because if you had a swimming pool and then basketball courts They have a,

01:09:13.619 --> 01:09:16.835
I think, a track that goes above. For instance, I think we— again,

01:09:17.318 --> 01:09:20.502
this would be downtown. If we were ever to do a rec center, would there

01:09:20.534 --> 01:09:22.480
be a height restriction on that?

01:09:24.100 --> 01:09:27.938
Depends on what it looks like, right? So civic would be the main question

01:09:27.954 --> 01:09:29.342
and location, whether it's downtown.

01:09:31.331 --> 01:09:34.832
So— Well, again, you're talking about 2 different entities. Civic is us.

01:09:35.639 --> 01:09:39.240
That's a different thing than a— Yeah,

01:09:39.740 --> 01:09:42.860
it's for a use or an institutional use or a civic use. Civic would be

01:09:43.360 --> 01:09:47.310
everyone compared to a private, say, 501, right, or something of that nature.

01:09:47.440 --> 01:09:50.900
And so, and you could separate them. I just want to make sure that's clear

01:09:51.400 --> 01:09:55.520
on the civic one. Um, so we're good?

01:09:56.020 --> 01:09:59.220
Okay, so here's my plan. Correct me if I'm wrong. We're going to

01:09:59.720 --> 01:10:02.450
look at other buildings, whether it's schools,

01:10:02.800 --> 01:10:06.293
see what their heights are. See if it's feasible to drop it down or

01:10:06.309 --> 01:10:06.542
comfortable.

01:10:09.852 --> 01:10:13.385
Possible code amendment, whether it's to separate if there's a

01:10:13.885 --> 01:10:17.024
recreational aspect to these buildings or standalone building,

01:10:17.963 --> 01:10:21.127
that could be adjusted. But then

01:10:21.627 --> 01:10:25.570
the other 2 items, we could do a development agreement. I think we're looking for

01:10:26.070 --> 01:10:29.353
a narrow scope of that, and then if not, to Melissa's point,

01:10:29.675 --> 01:10:33.030
then it maybe needs to be dealt with in an MDA. But I think

01:10:33.530 --> 01:10:36.690
that you can— we should be able to find a path through so

01:10:37.190 --> 01:10:40.350
that anybody else that comes in a similar situation where they're trying to do

01:10:40.850 --> 01:10:44.290
recreational use, that we have a standard outside the Civic,

01:10:44.790 --> 01:10:47.760
because the Civic is us, and we have different rules for the city.

01:10:49.120 --> 01:10:51.400
So, Mayor, can I ask one more question?

01:10:53.170 --> 01:10:56.230
Yeah, go ahead. So the question is this: having,

01:10:56.730 --> 01:11:00.258
having had some conversations, or at least listened to the DRC meeting. I think one

01:11:00.758 --> 01:11:04.191
of the concerns in the applicant that I heard from the applicant is just

01:11:04.271 --> 01:11:07.643
the timing of this. They're anxious to get started. And so

01:11:08.044 --> 01:11:11.351
I think if there's— and look,

01:11:11.961 --> 01:11:15.268
I, I, I, I think what the council is saying makes a

01:11:15.768 --> 01:11:19.266
lot of sense, so let me start there. But I think really he's going

01:11:19.766 --> 01:11:22.091
to walk away from this meeting and he's going to make a determination. Okay,

01:11:22.734 --> 01:11:25.830
if I, uh, if I, if I If I have

01:11:26.330 --> 01:11:28.830
to meet the height requirement, then I'm going to have to design my building in

01:11:29.330 --> 01:11:32.150
such a way that it's 35 feet if I want to get started right away,

01:11:32.650 --> 01:11:35.570
because this process that we're talking about is going to take a little while to

01:11:36.070 --> 01:11:39.970
get to a place where it might function for them. And so

01:11:40.470 --> 01:11:43.700
then the question remains in my mind, then is the council willing to entertain

01:11:43.830 --> 01:11:47.630
a development agreement for the, the wall

01:11:48.130 --> 01:11:51.898
that's just flat that's against Walmart and for the— Absolutely. Crossing guard issues.

01:11:51.963 --> 01:11:55.130
I think those are the questions that we just need to be really clear about.

01:11:55.634 --> 01:11:59.019
Sounds like the height is the hangup, but the other 2 are not, perhaps.

01:12:01.831 --> 01:12:05.527
Is it fair that if I said— now we don't have a lot of

01:12:06.027 --> 01:12:09.170
closed session items, maybe just a little bit, so we can go a little longer.

01:12:09.251 --> 01:12:12.359
But if this requires a little more attention and we need to massage this,

01:12:12.715 --> 01:12:16.179
could we move it to item— I used to always call it item 19.

01:12:16.540 --> 01:12:20.050
But we can maybe come back to this and give it

01:12:20.550 --> 01:12:23.170
the time it needs, or— I mean, it's up to you guys if you think

01:12:23.670 --> 01:12:25.890
we can get there. Otherwise,

01:12:26.390 --> 01:12:29.850
we can put a pin in it. I just want to

01:12:30.350 --> 01:12:32.509
know for sake of time what you guys— if you want to try to hammer

01:12:33.009 --> 01:12:35.690
it out right now, if we can get there, or do you want to— I

01:12:36.190 --> 01:12:38.790
would say no, it's not on the agenda. So I think we need to give

01:12:39.290 --> 01:12:41.790
him his instruction and let him go find that information and come back to us.

01:12:42.026 --> 01:12:45.568
As an agenda item. I was just going to see if

01:12:45.584 --> 01:12:48.948
there was a way to find out the numbers during the break,

01:12:48.964 --> 01:12:52.474
but also if we are going down the code road,

01:12:52.862 --> 01:12:56.183
it's going to have to come back, it'll go to planning, then 10

01:12:56.683 --> 01:13:00.660
days from that it'll come notice for us. Like, we're looking at at least

01:13:01.160 --> 01:13:04.137
2 months out if we do code for this, which is fine if that's what

01:13:04.637 --> 01:13:08.393
the will of the body is, but if we want to help them move

01:13:08.409 --> 01:13:11.734
forward with a development agreement, that's,

01:13:11.959 --> 01:13:15.861
I guess, the question. But if this is

01:13:15.893 --> 01:13:19.635
what it's going to take, I think the question that Mayor was asking us,

01:13:19.747 --> 01:13:23.216
though, you guys, is wall and pathways. And I

01:13:24.164 --> 01:13:27.199
do not care about the height of the wall or the pathways. Not the

01:13:27.699 --> 01:13:31.647
height of the wall, but the look of the wall. So for me,

01:13:31.872 --> 01:13:35.769
yes, absolutely, I could do a development agreement for Maybe

01:13:36.269 --> 01:13:39.700
everyone else can weigh in. Let me throw one other question out there real quick

01:13:39.732 --> 01:13:42.887
to the council, because— so what's preventing— let's say,

01:13:43.696 --> 01:13:47.322
assuming that Cedar Pass Ranch had no HOA

01:13:47.499 --> 01:13:50.995
