01:47:49.350 --> 01:47:53.060
the city by you know reviewing each kind of project on a case-by-case

01:47:53.560 --> 01:47:57.223
basis to see when it makes sense to have work occur off hours while

01:47:57.239 --> 01:47:59.918
still maintaining your guys being kept in the loop.

01:48:00.725 --> 01:48:04.279
This would reduce project delays as far as getting projects

01:48:04.779 --> 01:48:07.232
out to bid, issuing contracts, things of that nature.

01:48:10.000 --> 01:48:13.710
So some of the criteria that's in the code. It does

01:48:14.210 --> 01:48:17.760
prioritize public safety first, so when we're doing offsite work,

01:48:17.810 --> 01:48:21.530
we would look at things as traffic flow management. For example, there's a project

01:48:22.030 --> 01:48:25.790
coming up this summer at SR 73 and Ranches, which we're

01:48:26.290 --> 01:48:29.650
going to recommend for nighttime work because we know that's a very busy intersection and

01:48:30.150 --> 01:48:33.330
we don't want to try and reduce congestion there that's already

01:48:33.830 --> 01:48:37.390
present. This would also look at material placement, utility ties-in.

01:48:37.814 --> 01:48:41.063
And just trying to minimize impacts to the public and just safety in general.

01:48:42.216 --> 01:48:45.367
Some of the safeguards we have imposed is that it gives authority to the city

01:48:45.867 --> 01:48:49.379
engineer, also requiring you all to be notified prior to work

01:48:49.879 --> 01:48:53.002
started. Then it also has a provision there

01:48:53.502 --> 01:48:56.870
about notifying property residents

01:48:57.370 --> 01:49:01.057
and businesses in the area. And then, as I mentioned, it also adds a provision

01:49:01.557 --> 01:49:05.800
for emergency work, which is limited to city and utility-related operations.

01:49:05.810 --> 01:49:07.950
So, you know, your neighbor Joe can't go dig up his driveway in the middle

01:49:08.450 --> 01:49:11.770
of the night. So that's kind of all I've got

01:49:12.270 --> 01:49:14.080
for that code section. Happy to answer any questions.

