02:37:07.949 --> 02:37:11.862
Hello. So I'm here to speak about

02:37:11.974 --> 02:37:14.402
the extension of the road in Silver Lake,

02:37:15.215 --> 02:37:18.600
the neighborhood, Silver Lake Parkway. I just want to

02:37:19.100 --> 02:37:22.620
start by sharing my appreciation for all that you guys do for the city.

02:37:23.120 --> 02:37:25.700
I know that you guys have a pretty thankless job and that you guys put

02:37:26.200 --> 02:37:28.200
in a lot of hours, so thank you for all that you guys do for

02:37:28.700 --> 02:37:32.580
our city. I understand the concerns regarding increased

02:37:33.080 --> 02:37:36.200
traffic on our major neighborhood roadways, including Golden Eagle Road.

02:37:36.700 --> 02:37:39.840
My own house sits very close to Golden Eagle, and I'm out there driving it

02:37:40.340 --> 02:37:43.390
most mornings between 7 and 7:30. I know firsthand what the current

02:37:43.890 --> 02:37:47.950
flow looks like, and in my view, absorbing more traffic is absolutely worth it.

02:37:48.450 --> 02:37:51.930
We simply cannot expect a brand new high school to function safely or effectively

02:37:52.430 --> 02:37:56.510
without— with only one way in or out. Beyond traffic disruption,

02:37:57.010 --> 02:38:00.250
this extension is a matter of student safety. Right now, it is practically impossible for

02:38:00.750 --> 02:38:04.030
students to safely walk or bike to the new campus due to the lack

02:38:04.530 --> 02:38:06.730
of sidewalks on the south side of Pony Express Parkway.

02:38:07.950 --> 02:38:12.195
Our kids deserve safe and dedicated routes to school. This extension provides

02:38:12.695 --> 02:38:16.084
exactly that while simultaneously giving us an entire

02:38:16.570 --> 02:38:19.486
neighborhood a vital route in and out of our neighborhood.

02:38:20.870 --> 02:38:24.373
For the safety of our students and the long-term infrastructure of our community,

02:38:24.389 --> 02:38:26.908
please consider extending Silver Lake Parkway.

